      "title": "Scientific Integrity",
      "gist": "The missing ingredient is a leaning-over-backwards honesty: report everything that might doubt your result, since truth emerges eventually, and fooling yourself is the first danger.",
      "question": "Scientific integrity — what does it demand beyond not lying? (a principle with examples)"
    },
